      "description": "accepted minus handled. Non-zero means nginx accepted a connection and then dropped it without handling it \u2014 effectively always a resource limit (worker_connections, file descriptors). This is the one genuine saturation signal stub_status offers, and it should sit at 0 forever on a host this size.",
